PROPOSED CHANGE, NOT APPLIED -- the thermal display intent
==========================================================

STATUS: PROPOSAL. Nothing in this patch is applied to the working tree, and
nothing under sdk/ was written by the lane that produced it. The control-room
server was running at pid 654212 throughout and was not restarted, signalled or
touched.

Prepared by:   heat-transfer lab-lane, 2026-09-01
Base commit:   the router hunk is cut against sdk/chief_engineer/router.py at
               the HEAD named in the design note beside this file; verify with
               `git apply --check` before reading further.
Reviewers:     heat-transfer supervisor (reads it as a diff, SUPERVISION §3
               check 1), then the cfd team, because sdk/chief_engineer/ is
               shared control-room tooling owned by neither team and the
               routing table it changes governs every team's prompts.
Design note:   docs/campaigns/T-family/demo/PROPOSED_thermal_intent_NOTE.md
               Read the note first. It carries the measured before/after
               routing table and the restart procedure.

WHAT THIS PATCH DOES
  1. Adds a `thermal-display` intent to the router: a thermal question about a
     body whose run has ALREADY LANDED is answered by presenting that run.
  2. Adds `sdk/workflows/thermal_display.py`, which presents landed figures,
     tables and instrument checks. It starts no solver, writes no case, queues
     no job and books no compute.
  3. Adds `THERMAL_DISPLAY` to `_SURFACE_KEEPS_ROUTE`. This is load-bearing,
     not cosmetic: the thermal acts open with an upload, and without it
     `apply_surface` converts the route into a geometry study and points the
     incompressible aerodynamic chain at a body someone asked a thermal
     question about. Measured: at HEAD, both act prompts with an uploaded
     surface become `geometry-study`.

WHAT THIS PATCH DOES NOT DO
  * It does not add, remove or edit a single character of
    `_OUT_OF_SCOPE_DOMAINS`. The refusal list is untouched. See the note for
    why no edit to it is needed, and for the measured evidence that the list is
    consulted only on the no-workflow fallback path.
  * It does not solve anything, queue anything, or invoke a solver.
  * It does not touch `server.py`, `control_room.html`, or any other module.

WHAT THE ROUTER STILL REFUSES AFTER THIS PATCH
  Every prompt refused at HEAD is refused after this patch, unchanged, because
  the refusal path is unchanged. Specifically, a thermal request that names no
  body this lab has actually run scores nothing on the new intent and keeps the
  route it has today. Measured, still reaching the refusal path after the
  patch:
    "Do a thermal analysis of the motor and tell me the peak temperature."
    "Nusselt number on the cooling channel."
    "Simulate boiling in the coolant loop."
    "Simulate how the cube melts in a fire."
    "Model the combustion in the chamber."
  A KNOWN PRE-EXISTING DEFECT THIS PATCH DOES NOT FIX, and the reviewers must
  see it: three thermal prompts that SHOULD refuse do not refuse at HEAD
  either, because they route to `unseen-geometry`, which has a workflow, so the
  refusal list is never consulted for them. They behave identically before and
  after:
    "Run a conjugate heat transfer study on a rocket nozzle I am designing."
    "Do a thermal stress analysis of the turbine blade."
    "Model the heat transfer on the wing."
  That is a defect in the refusal ARCHITECTURE, not in the refusal LIST, and it
  is not this patch's to repair. It is written up in the design note for the
  cfd and verification teams.

